HST Office: new workbooks in Sheets use Excel's default size, 11 pt. Writer stays Times New Roman 12.

- ScDocShell::InitNew: the Default cell style of a new document gets the size, not the pool default, so a file that states
  no size keeps the old one and the user can still change the style. Filters also call InitNew before loading: they are
  left out, since oox skips a size equal to the pool default and would keep 11 for a 10 pt file. The empty rows follow at once.
- New sheets (ScDocFunc::InsertTable and the view's InsertTables, AppendTable, first-view sheets) get the same row height;
  sheets created while importing are left to the import.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-defaults.py.
---
--- a/sc/source/ui/docshell/docfunc.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/docshell/docfunc.cxx
@@ -1238,6 +1238,9 @@
 
     if (rDoc.InsertTab( nTab, rName ))
     {
+        // HST: a new sheet's empty rows follow the default style, like the first sheet's.
+        if (!rDoc.IsImportingXML())
+            rDocShell.AdjustRowHeight(0, rDoc.MaxRow(), nTab);
         if (bRecord)
             rDocShell.GetUndoManager()->AddUndoAction(
                         std::make_unique<ScUndoInsertTab>( rDocShell, nTab, bAppend, rName));
